      },
      "lineNbr": 114,
      "author": {
        "id": 1352056
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-18T18:13:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have found some instances on zephyr:\n- [espi_npcx.c](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/third_party/zephyr/main/drivers/espi/espi_npcx.c;l\u003d618)\n- [espi_it8xxx2.c](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/third_party/zephyr/main/drivers/espi/espi_it8xxx2.c;l\u003d1803)\n- [espi_mchp_xec.c](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/third_party/zephyr/main/drivers/espi/espi_mchp_xec.c;l\u003d858)\n\nThis is to inform the state of `eSPI Rese#` pin.",
      "parentUuid": "9d9e4369_d8dc74a3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 114,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 114,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "dc91fb7438722ac2bdb4ad004c5b503457d1527a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9769420e_a9b01b8e",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/ap_pwrseq/signal_vw.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 114,
      "author": {
        "id": 1352056
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-30T20:31:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "After further experimentation with different platforms, I would like to share some findings regarding this bus reset event:\n\n1. Although `event.evt_data` value is set with event `ESPI_BUS_RESET`, its interpretation does not seems to be standardized. For NPCX `event.evt_data \u003d 1` means that reset is asserted, and `0` means de-asserted. This logic is the opposite for ITE.\n\n2. ITE eSPI driver is using GPIO interruption to trigger `ESPI_BUS_RESET` (see function [espi_it8xxx2_enable_reset](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/third_party/zephyr/main/drivers/espi/espi_it8xxx2.c;l\u003d1812)) and for some reason, ISR is only called when GPD2 level goes high (reset logically de-asserted).\nAs a workaround, I configured GPD2 pin as `ACTIVE_LOW` in `zephyr/program/nissa/nereid/generated.dtsi`. This way, we get `ESPI_BUS_RESET` with `event.evt_data \u003d 0` and `vw_reset_all` is called.\n\nI would suggest that we make sure corresponding eSPI driver handles `evt_data` during this bus reset event uniformly.",
      "parentUuid": "ab65f6e6_ba9f8993",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 114,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 114,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "dc91fb7438722ac2bdb4ad004c5b503457d1527a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
